# Layout

Place Forge repos as **siblings** of the product project. Launchers default to `../<RepoName>`. Sibling clones plus a Node runtime are **how Forge actually runs**. The Vercel `forge-collection` server is the **map/gateway** Cursor talks to over HTTP; it does not vendor or execute those repos.

```text
parent/
  __PROJECT_ID__/          ← this product project
    scripts/*-mcp.sh
    .okf/
    .cursor/mcp.json       ← gitignored HTTP forge-collection (default)
  ForgeLifecycleContracts/
  ForgeRelay/
  ConceptForge/
  GovernanceForge/
  BuildForge/
  LaunchForge/             ← entry: mcp-server/dist/index.js
  OperateForge/
  CustomerForge/
  GrowthForge/
  RevenueForge/
  InsightForge/
  SunsetForge/
```

# Cursor MCP (Desktop vs Cloud)

Default project example `.cursor/mcp-forge-lifecycle.json.example` registers HTTP:

`https://forge-collection-mcp-server-nicksinxs-projects.vercel.app/api/mcp`

| Client | How to attach |
|--------|----------------|
| Cursor Desktop | User MCP (`~/.cursor/mcp.json`) **and/or** project `.cursor/mcp.json` |
| Cursor Cloud Agents | Custom HTTP URL on cursor.com/agents (same `/api/mcp`). Cloud **does not** see `~/.cursor/mcp.json` and does not inherit Desktop MCP |

Stdio siblings: `.cursor/mcp-forge-stdio-siblings.json.example` — only on a host that has clones and built `dist/`.

# Clone helper

From project root:

```bash
scripts/forge-clone-siblings.sh
```

Override org: `scripts/forge-clone-siblings.sh --org your-org`

# Overrides

When siblings are not peers, export per-server roots before starting MCP:

```bash
export LAUNCHFORGE_ROOT=/path/to/LaunchForge
export FORGERELAY_ROOT=/path/to/ForgeRelay
```

# Build requirement

Each sibling must be built before MCP start (`npm ci && npm run build`). Launchers fail fast with actionable messages when `dist/index.js` is missing.

